    "teacher_markdown": "**What Students Should Take Away:**\r\n\r\n- Students use `groupby()`, `size()`, and `unstack()` to count anime titles by stream type and score range.\r\n- Students compare both the total number of titles for each stream type and the score-range segments within each total.\r\n\r\n**Misconceptions Students Might Have or Points They Might Struggle With and Tips to Assist:**\r\n\r\n- Students may think `size()` calculates the average anime score.\r\n  - Tip: Explain that `size()` counts titles in each stream-type and score-range group.\r\n- Students may assume that a taller bar means a stream type has higher-scoring anime.\r\n  - Tip: Reinforce that total bar height represents the number of titles. Students must examine the individual score-range segments to discuss scores.\r\n- Students may overlook small segments because most titles fall below a score of 8.0.\r\n  - Tip: Direct students to use the legend and compare the `8.0–8.9` and `9.0–9.9` segments carefully. AI Tutor can help explain the grouped output or chart code without answering the data question.",
    "display_name": "Anime Scores",
    "bubble_choice_description": "Practice creating a **stacked bar chart** to answer a question about anime title scores across different stream types!",
